  "semantics": "Aggregate one current table into native variables output 0. Numeric integer/real: sum,count,min,max,avg,median,mode,standard_deviation,unique_count,null_count,first,last,only,concat. String: count,min,max,mode,unique_count,null_count,first,last,only,concat. Boolean/datetime/Variant: the same except concat. count includes NULL; unique_count excludes NULL; null_count counts NULL. median and sample SD return real. only is NULL for several distinct values. concat returns string, skips NULL, retains empty strings; proposal supports native defaults only: comma, no wrapper, unique=true, no sorting. Native output order follows field order then the enum below; one function keeps field name, several use native suffixes. Read real names/labels/types/values; no table output or training. Variant scalar output requires an owner-approved shared exact reader and contract before implementation.",
